 "summary": "Commodities were broadly weaker in the latest session, with 10 of the 24 tracked benchmarks higher and 12 lower. Energy fell across the board, led by Natural Gas at -1.50% to 2.56 USD/MMBtu; precious metals were mixed, 0 of 5 higher, the biggest move coming from Palladium at -2.73% to 998.00 USD/t oz; base metals were mixed, 5 of 6 higher, the biggest move coming from Copper at +1.10% to 6.58 USD/Lbs; bulk and battery materials were mixed, 2 of 5 higher, the biggest move coming from Rare Earth Elements at -2.17% to 37.47 USD/share; agriculture was mixed, 3 of 4 higher, the biggest move coming from Sugar at +0.66% to 19.23 USd/Lbs. The largest single move across the complex was Palladium at -2.73%. Uranium (U3O8) has not refreshed past the prior day's print and is flagged accordingly, being fixed periodically rather than traded continuously. Rare earths are represented by the MP Materials equity proxy, as no reliable daily spot benchmark is published. Reported alongside the session, Business Standard on 27 October 2026:",
